.TH HD-NETWORK-RENDER 8 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-network-render \- render the systemd-networkd files from the hyprdebian configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-network-render
.RB [ \-n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-network-render
reads the key
.B hd-network
in
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
and renders the
.BR systemd-networkd (8)
files in
.I /etc/systemd/network
from the jinja2 templates in
.IR /usr/share/hd-network/templates .
See
.BR hd-network (7)
for the settings.
.PP
Run it as root, after changing the settings with
.BR hd-network-iface (8)
or
.BR hd-network-bridge (8).
.SH OPERATION
.IP 1. 4
The settings are checked first.
An error stops the run before anything changes.
.IP 2. 4
A bridge without a MAC address gets a random one, which is stored in the
settings with
.BR hd-config-update (8).
.IP 3. 4
The files are written:
.RS
.TP
.I 30-<bridge>.netdev
makes the bridge, with its MAC address;
.TP
.I 40-<bridge>.network
the addresses of the bridge;
.TP
.I 50-<interface>.network
an interface with an exact name: its addresses, or the bridge it is a
port of;
.TP
.I 59-<glob>.network
an interface named by a glob, with the characters other than letters,
digits,
.BR . ,
.B _
and
.B \-
replaced by
.BR _ .
.RE
.IP
Only files whose content changes are written.
.IP 4. 4
Every file starts with a header that says it was generated.
A file in
.I /etc/systemd/network
with that header that the settings no longer ask for is removed.
Files without the header are left alone.
.IP 5. 4
When
.B wait_online
is set,
.B systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
is masked or unmasked to match.
.IP 6. 4
When files changed and systemd-networkd runs, it is reloaded with
.BR "networkctl reload" .
.PP
A reload applies new and changed
.I .network
files, but does not change a bridge that already exists, such as its MAC
address; that takes a reboot, or
.B networkctl delete
of the bridge followed by another reload.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show the files that would be written and removed, and what would happen to
the wait-online service, and change nothing.
A bridge without a MAC address shows a random one that is not stored.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the files were rendered, 1 on an error, 2 on wrong arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/network
Where the files are rendered.
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-network/templates
The jinja2 templates.
.SH EXAMPLES
See what a change of the settings would do, then apply it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hd-network-render \-\-dry\-run
hd-network-render
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-network (7),
.BR hd-network-iface (8),
.BR hd-network-bridge (8),
.BR hd-config-update (8),
.BR networkctl (1),
.BR systemd.network (5)
